"REL-01","PROTAGONIST","WOLF","A lone survival player and his tamed companion share an ordinary homestead routine.","The protagonist initially treats the wolf as one secure part of the structure he controls, while its obedience makes it unable to escape the later pen alone.","He tamed the wolf, built its pen beside the house and routinely seats it before mining.","At first he wants the wolf safely contained within his authored home; under pressure he wants it to trust and follow him beyond that home.","Expressed behaviourally, the wolf wants proximity, clear release and a traversable route.","The protagonist controls seating, gate access and route choice; the fire reverses this by making the wolf’s vulnerability control his final allocation of time.","The empty future pen conceals that the older protagonist has already rescued the wolf and kept it below the ridge sight line.","Possession within a protected structure becomes chosen responsibility after the structure is lost."

